# R15.14.1 local full-suite environment diagnosis — 2026-09-27

The first complete Control-suite run executed 657 tests. The new and focused
R15.14.1 tests were GREEN. One expected platform test was skipped. Three tests
failed:

- one R15.12 manifest assertion correctly detected that the current controller
  SHA-256 changed with `FINAL_CONTROL_TAG`;
- two historical S10.2D simulator tests reported the shared bounded code
  `SIMULATOR_LISTENER_SCENARIO_RED`.

Read-only reproduction of the listener subprocess showed the local checkout
had no Application `.venv` and the system Python lacked the pinned `psycopg`
dependency. The subprocess therefore stopped before opening its isolated
localhost test listener. This is a local test-runtime dependency gap, not a
source, listener-contract, product or server failure. No S10.2D source is
changed.

The R15.12 current-controller binding is updated to the freshly calculated
controller SHA-256. Python 3.9 cannot resolve the pinned dependency, so the
full suite is rerun with the bundled Python 3.12 workspace runtime and the
Application's exact pinned `psycopg[binary]==3.3.4` installed into a private
temporary test-only dependency directory. That directory is outside both
repositories and is not part of any release, runtime or deployment. The rerun
is GREEN: 657 tests, one expected platform skip.
